Package: throtl
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-venv, nethogs, iproute2
Recommends: rfkill
Maintainer: Flenser42 <105233392+Flenser42@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/Flenser42/throtl
Description: Per-application bandwidth limits and traffic prioritisation
 Throtl brings fine-grained bandwidth control to Linux: per-application
 download/upload limits and traffic priorities from a desktop dashboard
 (Tauri) or a scriptable CLI.
 .
 It is a thin layer on top of TrafficToll (tc/cgroups shaping) and nethogs
 (live per-process bandwidth). The privileged daemon runs as root via systemd
 and talks to the dashboard/CLI over a local Unix socket (no network port).
